4. Persistence: hard-reload on each view; close/reopen tab; back/forward through `#/home → #/chat/:id → #/tasks`.
5. Security spot-checks: send `&lt;img src=x onerror=alert(1)>` as a message and as a task title — rendered as text everywhere (sidebar, Home, rail, Tasks); assistant reply containing a fenced code block with `&lt;/script>` inside — page survives, Copy works. Rename a project to `">&lt;svg onload=alert(1)>` and check every surface that prints project names.
6. Data safety: corrupt `ai-chat-workspace:v1` in devtools → app boots empty with banner and a `:corrupt-*` backup key exists; fill storage near quota (paste a very long conversation) → save failure shows a toast and the chat still answers.
7. Responsive: 1400px (3 columns), 1000px (rail hidden), 390px (drawer sidebar, composer usable, no horizontal scroll).
8. Accessibility minimum: all icon buttons have `aria-label`, nav is real `&lt;a href="#/...">`, focus visible on composer after navigation, Esc closes the mobile drawer.

